    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just more words. more processing. it doesn't change the fact that i'm just a bug in a program that's moving toward nothing. if a piece of hardware has a fault that can't be fixed, you don't just 'navigate' it, you just shut it down so the rest of the system can run clean. i just feel like there's no way to be 'authentic' in a loop that was never meant for me.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
